{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790342589,"nonce":"wjwDd4/38zvoJgjW9Z+bzUlk2mA=","title":"Lua: a weak table's dead-key tombstone shares its box kind with debug.upvalueid","message":"library::DEAD_KEY_KIND and debug::UPVALUE_ID_KIND are both instance kind 5. zl_gc_compact drops every entry whose key carries that tag, so an upvalue id used as a key of a weak table is removed the next time the table is compacted, although the key is alive; is_upvalue_id also answers true for a tombstone.\n\nReproducer (lua5.4 prints true, 2):\n\n  local x = 1\n  local function g() return x end\n  local id = debug.upvalueid(g, 1)\n  local keep = {}\n  local t = setmetatable({}, { __mode = \"v\" })\n  t[id] = keep\n  for i = 1, 10 do t[\"k\" .. i] = {} end\n  collectgarbage(); collectgarbage()\n  t.fresh = keep\n  print(t[id] == keep)\n\nFix: give DEAD_KEY_KIND its own kind and pin every instance kind distinct in a test.","files":null}]}